WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:05.360
Let’s ask a philosophical question: What
is it that makes up a person’s soul?

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:11.639
Is it their personality, their memories, their
emotions, the history of their good and bad

00:00:11.639 --> 00:00:12.679
deeds?

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:17.910
Is it an energy that inhabits a living body,
an active consciousness, or even all of the

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:18.910
above?

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:23.169
Or is the soul just an entirely nebulous and
undefinable concept?

00:00:23.169 --> 00:00:28.769
The idea of the soul is almost as old as human
civilization itself, with philosophers from

00:00:28.769 --> 00:00:34.329
as far back as Ancient Greece and even before
acknowledging its existence..

00:00:34.329 --> 00:00:39.960
Numerous religions from all over the world,
if not all of them, also hold teachings about

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.420
the nature of souls, even though they might
vary.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:48.790
For example, Judaism and some denominations
of Christianity state that only human beings

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:54.060
have an immortal soul that will live on in
Heaven after a person’s death, and the end

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.870
of their time on Earth.

00:00:55.870 --> 00:01:01.469
Meanwhile, certain Catholic theologians - meaning,
people who study religion - claim that a soul

00:01:01.469 --> 00:01:03.990
inhabits all living creatures.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:09.000
And so, the philosophical and theological
debate goes on, with the general consensus

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.270
being that souls are… well, they’re a
little bit of everything.

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:18.310
Every part of someone that makes them who
they are: character, emotions, reasoning,

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:22.330
consciousness, memories, and thoughts all
blended together.

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:27.710
But if we accept that a soul is something
that exists, then is it something that can

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:28.880
be altered?

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:31.550
Is it constant or can it be manipulated?

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:35.700
Could a person’s soul even be removed entirely?

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:41.000
At first glance, SCP-158 appears to be a device
resembling a mechanical arm.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:45.930
In fact, it’s a lot like the kind of machine
you might expect to find inside a huge factory,

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:50.780
standing as part of an assembly line, welding
and drilling components together day in and

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:52.110
day out.

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:57.590
This particular mechanized arm, however, features
a number of unique and bizarre differences

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:00.580
from any currently used in automated production.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:06.700
For starters, it has an unusual attachment
at one end, a three-pronged, tridactyl-like

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:07.700
claw.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:12.459
The arm itself is also designed to be suspended
from the ceiling, ideally hanging upside down

00:02:12.459 --> 00:02:14.750
in a room big enough to accommodate it.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:20.540
There is a long series of winding cables connecting
SCP-158 to a complicated computer console

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:25.310
that is used to control the device, while
the remaining cables are intended to be connected

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:27.020
to a power source.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:31.209
As for the console, it possesses a visual
display unit and a keyboard like you might

00:02:31.209 --> 00:02:37.129
expect it to, and at the bottom there is what
appears to be some form of a dispenser, seemingly

00:02:37.129 --> 00:02:42.409
designed to attach to a container of some
kind, measuring three inches wide by seven

00:02:42.409 --> 00:02:43.980
inches tall.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:48.930
The ideal receptacle to fit the attachment
is that of a glass jar or beaker.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:54.620
This mechanical arm was first uncovered by
the Foundation in late 2007, inside a burned-down

00:02:54.620 --> 00:03:00.159
hospital in an unknown location that has been
redacted from the SCP-158 file.

00:03:00.159 --> 00:03:05.230
The hospital itself was derelict, abandoned,
and appeared to have been unused for a considerable

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:09.849
period of time, approximately five years but
perhaps more.

00:03:09.849 --> 00:03:15.530
Agents working for the Foundation recovered
SCP-158, along with an owner’s manual that

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:21.069
presumably would have contained detailed instructions
describing the device’s function and exactly

00:03:21.069 --> 00:03:22.830
how to operate it.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:27.579
This manual had been badly damaged by the
fire, but the readable portions of it were

00:03:27.579 --> 00:03:32.379
later transcribed and copied, and now a single
copy of what was left of the manual is kept

00:03:32.379 --> 00:03:35.420
with SCP-158 at all times.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:41.549
While most instructions detailing the operation
of SCP-158 did survive and were able to be

00:03:41.549 --> 00:03:46.139
copied, any chapters that might have explained
who built it or what it actually did were

00:03:46.139 --> 00:03:49.900
too badly damaged to read, lost to the fire.

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:55.959
Much like the owner’s manual, all components
of SCP-158 - the arm, the console, and the

00:03:55.959 --> 00:04:01.249
cables - have all appeared to sustain some
amount of fire damage, but remain intact and

00:04:01.249 --> 00:04:03.159
in full working order.

00:04:03.159 --> 00:04:08.129
The damage is only cosmetic, and while it
might take around twenty minutes to boot up,

00:04:08.129 --> 00:04:11.319
this fire damage doesn’t affect the machine’s
function.

00:04:11.319 --> 00:04:17.600
But the question still remains: what exactly
is the intended purpose of this mechanical

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:18.600
arm?

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:23.060
Well, through a long process of trial and
error, and following the surviving portions

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:27.140
of the manual, the Foundation was able to
get the device working again.

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:32.200
They learned that SCP-158 will only perform
its function when presented with an ordinary

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.670
living being.

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:38.260
While human beings, namely members of Class
D personnel, are typically used as test subjects

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:42.870
by the Foundation, this actually applies to
any living creature that has the ability to

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:48.130
display cognition, which is the mental process
of gaining knowledge, in order to perform

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:52.170
cognitive functions like thinking, remembering
and problem-solving.

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:58.840
When a person, or other non-human being, possessing
cognition is presented to SCP-158, the machine

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:03.770
will then go to work, and extract an unknown,
gas-based substance from them.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:09.170
This substance is then deposited in the jar
or beaker that is fitted to the dispenser

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:10.770
beneath the console.

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:12.870
So, what does it take?

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:18.100
Is it some sort of advanced form of decontamination
device, removing all toxins and impurities

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.100
from a body?

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.280
Oh, if only that were true.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:27.970
Sadly, you see, the Foundation didn’t give
SCP-158 the nickname of the “Soul Extractor”

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:29.210
for nothing.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:33.640
After the machine has performed its function,
the now formerly cognitive organism on the

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:38.420
receiving end will display a complete and
total loss of their higher brain functions.

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:43.890
They won’t be able to speak, form coherent
thoughts, or even remember who they were before

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:46.610
SCP-158 was switched on.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:52.190
The device will rob them of any and all parts
of themselves, essentially leaving the person

00:05:52.190 --> 00:06:00.020
or creature as a hollowed-out shell, a husk
of their previous self, a body without a soul.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:05.590
Perhaps even crueler though, is that this
extraction process is not fatal, and victims

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:08.060
are left alive afterward.

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:13.270
They no longer possess their capability for
cognitive thought, and will not respond to

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:15.860
any form of external stimuli around them.

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:20.420
There has been some level of brain stem activity
recorded in most cases, and subjects have

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:25.760
been known to exhibit basic reflexes, but
this is the only active movement that they

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:27.570
are now capable of.

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:30.970
As for that substance that test subjects have
removed from their bodies?

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:36.840
Well, it takes the form of gas, as we mentioned
earlier, but it also seems to be comprised

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:41.120
of a mixture of kinetic, electrical, heat,
and light energy.

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:46.590
In fact, each jar of the substance is an infinite
source of these various types of energy, albeit

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:50.460
only capable of a very low rate and output
on average.

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:55.740
The general consensus among Foundation researchers
is that this substance is the physical soul

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:58.450
that has been removed from a subject.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:02.640
So, do they stay stuck as soulless shells
forever?

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:08.390
Actually, SCP-158 is in fact capable of returning
the extracted substance to a subject that

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:10.390
it performed a removal on.

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:14.950
However, whether a test subject, normally
a member of D Class, receives their soul after

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:20.230
having it extracted is all down to whatever
test is being conducted by the Foundation.

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:24.720
Those that do get given their souls back will
usually regain access to all of their previously

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:29.960
lost cognition and higher brain functions,
but the rate at which they return can vary

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:31.970
depending on the subject.

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:36.170
Replacing the substance from one patient with
that of another can also cause these results

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:37.450
to differ.

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:42.790
And again, that’s if the SCP Foundation
even bothers to replace a test subject’s

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:45.680
soul, instead of just leaving them hollowed
out.

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:49.640
It’s actually pretty terrifying to think
that the Foundation has the freedom and the

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:55.030
capability to do that to somebody, taking
away everything that makes someone a human

00:07:55.030 --> 00:08:00.530
being, only to leave their soul in a jar while
their vacant body lives on without thought

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:02.000
or consciousness.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:07.390
It was due to the unique, anomalous function
of SCP-158 that the device was proposed to

00:08:07.390 --> 00:08:10.150
become part of a Foundation research endeavor.

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:15.420
Codenamed the “Olympia Project” and overseen
by its head researcher, Professor Kain Pathos

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:20.560
Crow, who has the head of a golden retriever,
but that’s a story for another day.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:25.070
The ultimate aim of the project was to use
the anomalous properties of a number of SCPs

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:29.750
to successfully create an artificial human
that would become a potential asset of the

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:31.490
SCP Foundation.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:36.659
As part of one series of Olympia Project experiments,
Professor Crow gathered a group of D Class

00:08:36.659 --> 00:08:40.990
personnel to undergo testing using SCP-158.

00:08:40.990 --> 00:08:45.790
Each of these individuals had been interviewed
by Crow himself and were selected based on

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:50.290
personality traits and characteristics that
the Professor liked or thought would be useful

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:53.199
to have in the Foundation’s artificial humanoid.

00:08:53.199 --> 00:08:58.270
The group chosen by Professor Crow featured
a mix of male and female test subjects, as

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:02.399
Crow believed “a soul transcends the flesh
it is interred in.”

00:09:02.399 --> 00:09:06.450
The main purpose of the experiment was to
try and uncover some of the further functions

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:12.649
of SCP-158, basically pushing the machine
to its limit, trying to learn more information

00:09:12.649 --> 00:09:17.490
about the device that would have been contained
in the damaged portions of the owner’s manual.

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:22.139
Professor Crow had pored over the sections
that had survived intact, making sure he knew

00:09:22.139 --> 00:09:27.560
every available piece of information on SCP-158
inside and out.

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:32.399
The obscured instructions he was able to decipher
were, according to his notes, “sketchy at

00:09:32.399 --> 00:09:34.980
best, and downright unhelpful at worst.”

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:38.920
Crow began his experiments by removing the
first subject’s soul and then trying to

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:43.560
use the device to do literally anything else
with the extracted substance.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:47.380
Despite trying everything he could think of,
the Professor learned there was little the

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:52.180
Soul Extractor could do with a soul once it
had been removed, other than reverse the process

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:55.930
and return the substance to the body it had
been taken from.

00:09:55.930 --> 00:10:00.389
By then repeating this with further D Class
test subjects, Crow was able to learn the

00:10:00.389 --> 00:10:05.301
exact input sequence needed to reverse a soul
extraction, whilst before this had only ever

00:10:05.301 --> 00:10:07.639
been achieved through blind luck.

00:10:07.639 --> 00:10:13.209
By his sixth experiment with SCP-158, Professor
Crow noticed there was a brief period in the

00:10:13.209 --> 00:10:17.699
middle of performing its function that the
device would pause as if awaiting further

00:10:17.699 --> 00:10:18.699
commands.

00:10:18.699 --> 00:10:23.480
Crow theorized that this pause was there for
additional sequences to be inputted via the

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:24.480
machine’s console.

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:29.809
He began removing and re-implanting the same
soul into the following test subject, both

00:10:29.809 --> 00:10:33.740
to practice but also experiment with the Soul
Extractor’s controls.

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:38.329
The Professor found it strange that, despite
what he was doing to her, the D Class suffered

00:10:38.329 --> 00:10:43.470
little to no side effects to her health, even
though her soul was being continually removed

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:44.790
and replaced.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:51.199
Then, on experiment number eleven, Crow seemed
to crack that little pause SCP-158 took during

00:10:51.199 --> 00:10:52.430
each operation.

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:58.350
A new list of commands appeared on the monitor,
like ‘split’, ‘merge’, ‘remove aspects’,

00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:01.209
‘add aspects’, and ‘combine aspects’.

00:11:01.209 --> 00:11:06.230
It seemed to the Professor that the device
could be used to not only remove souls but

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:07.439
alter them.

00:11:07.439 --> 00:11:11.309
Through his further experiments, Crow learned
that the ‘aspects’ the machine mentioned

00:11:11.309 --> 00:11:16.779
were elements of a person’s personality,
such as willpower, understanding, conscience,

00:11:16.779 --> 00:11:22.499
creativity, empathy; and the Soul Extractor
could be used to manipulate and rewrite a

00:11:22.499 --> 00:11:26.839
person’s entire identity, before placing
it back into their body.

00:11:26.839 --> 00:11:32.100
However, this took a considerable amount of
testing, causing Professor Crow to grow more

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:35.810
and more frustrated with the complex workings
of the device.

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:41.570
That was until he eventually realized it wasn’t
SCP-158 that was too complicated for its own

00:11:41.570 --> 00:11:42.570
good.

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:49.769
The machine was trying to quantify the unquantifiable,
explain something inexplicable: the very nature

00:11:49.769 --> 00:11:51.579
of the human soul.

00:11:51.579 --> 00:11:57.649
Professor Crow began using SCP-158 to modify
a composite soul, which he referred to as

00:11:57.649 --> 00:11:59.220
Subject Zero.

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:04.410
While working on it, he realized the soul
itself seemed to be aware of its surroundings,

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:08.520
possessing a level of knowledge above that
of most Foundation researchers, including

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:10.050
Crow himself.

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:15.660
Either by fluke or by meddling with SCP-158,
the Professor had created a soul that seemed

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:21.230
to exist on several planes of existence beyond
the physical world that we know.

00:12:21.230 --> 00:12:27.740
Subject Zero had become a sentient, disembodied
consciousness, an entity that could see, hear,

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:32.660
feel and think without the need for a physical
form or body to house it.

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:37.589
Zero was proposed to become Professor Crow’s
assistant, given that it displayed respect

00:12:37.589 --> 00:12:40.980
and admiration to him for having created it.

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:43.800
Almost like a child looking up to a father
figure.

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:48.459
All it asked in return was to be given a name
other than ‘Subject Zero’.

00:12:48.459 --> 00:12:52.350
Crow told the disembodied entity it could
name itself whatever it liked.

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:57.119
The Foundation then planned for the composite
soul, now formerly known as Subject Zero,

00:12:57.119 --> 00:13:02.249
to be a component of the Olympia Project’s
artificial humanoid, whenever its creation

00:13:02.249 --> 00:13:03.699
was successfully completed.

00:13:03.699 --> 00:13:06.529
Don’t you just love a happy ending?

00:13:06.529 --> 00:13:13.910
Now go check out “Living Ice Cream Van SCP-1386”
and “SCP-261 - Pan-Dimensional Vending Machine”

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:18.190
for more peculiar anomalous machines from
the SCP Foundation!

